#direction: right
#spacing: 10
#gravity: .8
#arrowSize: 4
#font: 'Open Sans'
#background: transparent
#fill: #f4f6fb
#title: cryptography1

[IDisposable|Provides a mechanism
for releasing unmanaged
resources]

[AsymmetricAlgorithm|
Represents the abstract base class from
which all implementations of asymmetric
algorithms must inherit.]

[DSA|
Represents the abstract base class from 
which all implementations of the 
Digital Signature Algorithm (DSA)
must inherit.]

[RSA|
Represents the base class from 
which all implementations of
the RSA algorithm inherit.]

[ECAlgorithm|
Represents the abstract class 
from which elliptic-curve asymmetric
algorithms can inherit.]

[ECDiffieHellman|
Provides an abstract base class that 
Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman (ECDH) 
algorithm implementations can derive from.]

[ECDSA|
Provides an abstract base class that 
encapsulates the Elliptic Curve
Digital Signature Algorithm (ECDSA).]

[SymmetricAlgorithm|
Represents the abstract base class from
which all implementations of symmetric 
algorithms must inherit.]

[Aes|
Represents the abstract base class 
from which all implementations of 
the Advanced Encryption Standard (AES)
must inherit.]

[DES|
Represents the base class for the Data 
Encryption Standard (DES) algorithm 
from which all DES implementations
must derive.]

[RC2|
Represents the base class from which
all implementations of the RC2 
algorithm must derive.]

[TripleDES|
Represents the base class for 
Triple Data Encryption Standard
algorithms from which all 
TripleDES implementations must derive.]

[IDisposable] <:-- [AsymmetricAlgorithm]
[AsymmetricAlgorithm] <:- [DSA]
[AsymmetricAlgorithm] <:- [ECAlgorithm]
[AsymmetricAlgorithm] <:- [RSA]
[ECAlgorithm] <:- [ECDiffieHellman]
[ECAlgorithm] <:- [ECDSA]

[IDisposable] <:-- [SymmetricAlgorithm] 
[SymmetricAlgorithm] <:- [Aes]
[SymmetricAlgorithm] <:- [DES]
[SymmetricAlgorithm] <:- [RC2]
[SymmetricAlgorithm] <:- [TripleDES]



